        612.0,
        792.0
      ],
      "native_blocks": [
        {
          "bbox": [
            48.0,
            278.0,
            560.5162353515625,
            397.3434143066406
          ],
          "text": "Some days later, while stalking his prey in the forest, the Lion was caught\nin the toils of a hunter's net. Unable to free himself, he filled the forest with\nhis angry roaring. The Mouse knew the voice and quickly found the Lion\nstruggling in the net. Running to one of the great ropes that bound him, she\ngnawed it until it parted, and soon the Lion was free.\n"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            48.0,
            617.0,
            284.27105712890625,
            644.2160034179688
          ],
          "text": "A kindness is never wasted.\n"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            48.0,
            691.0,
            346.8089904785156,
            703.365966796875
          ],
          "text": "Aesop | Illustration: Milo Winter (1919) | Source: Project Gutenberg #19994\n"
        },
